diff --git a/docs/drivers/freedreno.rst b/docs/drivers/freedreno.rst
index 60ab3e98c11..ccfccd197df 100644
--- a/docs/drivers/freedreno.rst
+++ b/docs/drivers/freedreno.rst
@@ -647,6 +647,30 @@ The best way to pinpoint the reg which causes a failure is to bisect the regs
 range. In case when a fail is caused by combination of several registers
 the ``inverse`` flag may be set to find the reg which prevents the failure.
 
+Command-stream storage on KGSL
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+Turnip pools command-stream storage in mapped 2 MiB BO slabs on KGSL. Independent
+streams own non-overlapping, page-aligned slices; read-only and GPU-writable
+storage use separate slabs. Large allocations remain dedicated BOs. Reset keeps
+only the last slice of each stream, returning overflow slices for reuse, and
+destroying a stream returns all of its slices. At most one empty slab per access
+class is retained to avoid repeated mapping churn.
+
+Set ``TU_DEBUG=noslabcs`` before starting the application to restore dedicated
+command-stream BO allocation for comparison. This allocation policy cannot be
+changed through ``TU_DEBUG_FILE`` while a device is running. ``TU_DEBUG=bos``
+reports both mapped parent slabs and live command-stream slices; slice counts
+must not be added to BO counts when estimating userspace mappings. Slabs reduce
+command-storage mappings, not mappings for application resources or imported
+memory.
+
+A native build with ``-Dbuild-tests=true`` provides ``tu_cs_slabs_test`` in the
+``turnip-cs`` Meson test suite. It exercises the production CS and slab allocator
+with a host-only BO backend, including slice reuse, borrowed IB offsets, reset,
+growth, allocation failures, concurrent owners, and bounded empty-slab caching.
+The test does not submit GPU work or replace device conformance testing.
+
 Runtime toggling of ``TU_DEBUG`` options
 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 
